# ── Supabase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a free project at https://supabase.com, then copy these from
# Project Settings → API. Paste into .env.local (never commit .env.local).
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-KEY

# Server-only — used by admin tasks / seeding scripts (Node, not the browser
# bundle). NEVER prefix with VITE_ and never commit the real value.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=YOUR-SERVICE-ROLE-KEY

# ── Student Google sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Students sign in with their college Google account. Enable the Google
# provider in Supabase (Authentication → Providers → Google) and add
# http://localhost:3000/auth/callback to the Redirect URLs — see README.
# The college Workspace domain students must use. Any address outside it is
# rejected by the OAuth callback. Defaults to pes.edu when unset.
# VITE_COLLEGE_DOMAIN=pes.edu

# ── Face verification service (optional hardening — FastAPI + DeepFace) ─
# Leave unset: in-browser descriptor capture + client matching is used.
# When set, enrolment/verification are proxied through the `face-verify`
# Supabase Edge Function so FACE_SERVICE_URL/FACE_SERVICE_TOKEN never reach
# the browser. Set these as Edge Function secrets, NOT as VITE_ vars:
#   supabase secrets set FACE_SERVICE_URL=... FACE_SERVICE_TOKEN=...
# Then flip this PUBLIC flag on so the app uses the server-side path (this is
# NOT a secret — it only toggles behaviour; the token stays in the functions):
# VITE_FACE_VERIFICATION=true
# The service itself lives in ./face-service — see face-service/README.md.
# FACE_SERVICE_URL=https://your-face-service.onrender.com
# FACE_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# ── Twilio parent SMS (Supabase Edge Function) ───────────────────────
# Secrets for the notify-shortfall edge function, set with
# `supabase secrets set …` (see supabase/functions/notify-shortfall/README.md).
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=+1XXXXXXXXXX
# TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=MGxxxxxxxx
